{
  "id": "cI-mvp-idea-agent-0001",
  "name": "CollaInsight - MVP - Idea Agent (Command Router)",
  "active": false,
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# CollaInsight — MVP Orchestration Workflow\n\n**n8n is the orchestration layer only. All intelligence lives in the Python backend (LangGraph agents).**\n\n```\nTelegram → n8n → Python Backend (LangGraph Agent) → Supabase → n8n → Telegram Reply\n```\n\nThis workflow:\n1. Receives every Telegram message.\n2. Keeps only slash-command messages (`/idea`, `/question`, ...) — the command IS the classification, no AI guessing here.\n3. Routes by command with a Switch node.\n4. `/idea` is the only command wired to real logic for the MVP — it calls the backend's `POST /api/idea` and relays the JSON reply back to Telegram.\n5. The other five commands (`/question`, `/suggestion`, `/decision`, `/action`, `/observation`) end at a **placeholder node** so the full six-agent architecture is visible on canvas during the presentation, even though only one agent is implemented.\n\nAdding a new agent later = swap its placeholder NoOp node for an HTTP Request node pointed at its own backend endpoint. No restructuring of this workflow required.",
        "height": 340,
        "width": 1080,
        "color": 6
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-40, -420],
      "id": "c011a000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "Sticky - Architecture Overview"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "updates": ["message"],
        "additionalFields": {}
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.telegramTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.5,
      "position": [0, 0],
      "id": "c011a000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "name": "Telegram Trigger",
      "webhookId": "b3f6d8c1-4e3b-4f7a-9c15-7b8e2d1a6f94",
      "credentials": {
        "telegramApi": {
          "id": "REPLACE_ME",
          "name": "🔧 REPLACE ME — Telegram Bot Credential"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "strict",
            "version": 3
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "1a2b3c4d-0001-4000-8000-000000000001",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.message.text }}",
              "rightValue": "",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "notEmpty",
                "singleValue": true
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "1a2b3c4d-0001-4000-8000-000000000002",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.message.text }}",
              "rightValue": "/",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "startsWith"
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.filter",
      "typeVersion": 2.3,
      "position": [260, 0],
      "id": "c011a000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
      "name": "Is Command"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "jsCode": "const msg = $json.message;\nconst text = (msg && msg.text || '').trim();\nconst parts = text.split(/\\s+/);\nconst command = (parts[0] || '').toLowerCase();\nconst content = parts.slice(1).join(' ').trim();\nconst from = msg.from || {};\n\nreturn {\n  json: {\n    command,\n    idea_text: content,\n    // Display-only attribution (matches 07_DATABASE_SCHEMA.md's MVP scope note:\n    // Telegram participants are identified by raw username/first name, not a\n    // persistent account ID - no account linking exists in the MVP).\n    telegram_display_name: from.username || from.first_name || 'unknown',\n    chat_id: msg.chat.id,\n    // Group name, not personal data - only present for groups/supergroups,\n    // not private chats (msg.chat.title is undefined there).\n    chat_title: msg.chat.title || null,\n    message_id: msg.message_id\n  }\n};"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [520, 0],
      "id": "c011a000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004",
      "name": "Parse Command"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "**Command Router**\nSwitch on `$json.command`. Only `/idea` is wired to a real branch. The other five outputs go straight to placeholder nodes below — no AI or logic runs for them in the MVP.",
